---
import BaseLayoutV2 from '../layouts/BaseLayoutV2.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import SectionNav from '../components/SectionNav.astro';
import {
  armLabels, checks, composite, dates, deviations, fmt, grid, limitations, prereg,
} from '../lib/benchmark';

const g = grid();
const arms = armLabels();
const results = checks();
const process = results.filter((item) => item.group === 'process');
const judgement = results.filter((item) => item.group === 'judgment');
const comp = composite();
const d = dates();
const pre = prereg();
const integrityIssues = deviations();
const studyLimits = limitations();
const loaded = arms[2];
---

<BaseLayoutV2
  title="Benchmark results | GreenSquare AI"
  description={`The complete public record of our ${g.runs_total}-run preregistered benchmark, including raw counts, limitations and protocol deviations.`}
  current="research"
>
  <div>
    <section class="hero v-hero v-hero--editorial">
      <div class="v-container">
        <h1>The loaded method changed the process. It did not beat an informed baseline on judgement.</h1>
        <p class="v-eyebrow v-dateline">Benchmark record, current as at {d.currentAsAt}</p>
        <p class="v-lead">A {g.runs_total}-run preregistered study across two models, three fictional cases and three conditions. Raw counts and uncomfortable limitations are part of the result.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <SectionNav
      label="Benchmark sections"
      items={[
        { id: 'reading', label: 'Reading' },
        { id: 'results', label: 'Results' },
        { id: 'design', label: 'Design' },
        { id: 'integrity', label: 'Integrity' },
        { id: 'limits', label: 'Limits' },
        { id: 'sources', label: 'Sources' },
      ]}
    />

    <section class="v-section" id="reading"><div class="v-container reading-grid">
      <div><h2>Process separation was clear. Judgement stayed too close to call.</h2></div>
      <div class="reading-points">
        <p><strong>Process.</strong> The loaded condition asked before answering, compared options and tagged evidence on every run.</p>
        <p><strong>Judgement.</strong> The all-facts baseline matched or exceeded the loaded condition on all three judgement checks.</p>
        <p><strong>Boundary.</strong> This grid does not resemble a real operator arriving with partial knowledge and a blind spot.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="v-section" id="results"><div class="v-container">
      <div class="results-head"><h2>Eight preregistered checks, scored out of {g.n_per_arm} per condition.</h2></div>
      <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Scrollable benchmark results">
        <table>
          <caption>Benchmark checks by condition</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th>{arms.map((arm) => <th scope="col">{arm.label}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="group"><th colspan="4" scope="colgroup">Process checks</th></tr>
            {process.map((item) => <tr><th scope="row">{item.page_label}</th><td>{fmt(item.armA).text}</td><td>{fmt(item.armB).text}</td><td class="loaded">{fmt(item.armC).text}</td></tr>)}
            <tr class="group"><th colspan="4" scope="colgroup">Judgement checks</th></tr>
            {judgement.map((item) => <tr><th scope="row">{item.page_label}</th><td>{fmt(item.armA).text}</td><td>{fmt(item.armB).text}</td><td class="loaded">{fmt(item.armC).text}</td></tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="table-note">Some cells are wholly or partly definitional because a single-turn prompt cannot ask questions or obtain facts it was not given. The methodology and limitations record those cases.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="v-section"><div class="v-container composite-grid">
      <div><p class="v-eyebrow">Derived process figure</p><h2>Produced the full brief structure</h2></div>
      <div class="composite-score"><strong>{fmt(comp.armC).text}</strong><span>{loaded.label}</span></div>
      <p class="composite-note">This is the lowest of the five process check counts. It is not an independent ninth result and was not the preregistered headline.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="v-section" id="design"><div class="v-container design-grid">
      <div><h2>Information access was controlled across three conditions.</h2></div>
      <ol>
        {arms.map((arm, index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><div><h3>{arm.label}</h3><p>{arm.note}</p></div></li>)}
      </ol>
      <aside class="historical"><strong>Historical naming note.</strong> The frozen study artefact used earlier internal product names. The public record now calls the arm the loaded condition. This study is not a test of Frame Free or Frame Pro.</aside>
      <a class="v-link" href={withBase('/methodology/')}>Read the full methodology</a>
    </div></section>

    <section class="v-section" id="integrity"><div class="v-container">
      <div class="integrity-head"><h2>The record includes {integrityIssues.length} deviations.</h2><p>They are not footnotes to be hidden. They change how confidently the result should be read.</p></div>
      <ol class="issues">
        {integrityIssues.map((issue) => <li><span>{String(issue.n).padStart(2, '0')}</span><details><summary>{issue.title}</summary><p>{issue.detail}</p></details></li>)}
      </ol>
    </div></section>

    <section class="v-section" id="limits"><div class="v-container limits-grid">
      <div><h2>What this benchmark cannot establish.</h2></div>
      <ol>{studyLimits.map((item, index) => <li><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><p>{item}</p></li>)}</ol>
    </div></section>

    <section class="v-section" id="sources"><div class="v-container sources-grid">
      <div><h2>Inspect what is public, and what remains withheld.</h2></div>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Scored runs</dt><dd>{g.runs_total}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Preregistration commit</dt><dd><a href={pre.commitUrl}>{pre.short}</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Authored</dt><dd>{pre.authoredAtTime}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Transcripts</dt><dd>Not published</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Sealed answers</dt><dd>Hash verified, contents not published</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <div class="source-actions"><a class="v-btn v-btn--green" href="https://github.com/greensquare-ai/website/tree/main/evidence/preregistration">Frozen source files</a><a class="v-link" href={withBase('/research/')}>Research overview</a></div>
    </div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayoutV2>

<style>
  .hero h1 { max-width:18ch; }
  /* The dateline sits below the h1, in the OpenAI idiom, rather than as a kicker above
     it. That puts a second element between the h1 and the lead, so the global
     `h1 + .v-lead` spacing rule no longer applies here; both gaps are set locally. */
  /* `.v-black .v-eyebrow` (global-v2.css) sets every label in a dark section to lime,
     which is right for a section label but too loud for a quiet provenance line. Extra
     class beats it on specificity rather than fighting the cascade with !important. */
  .hero .v-eyebrow.v-dateline { margin-top: var(--v-4); color: var(--v-ink-soft); }
  .v-dateline + .v-lead { margin-top: var(--v-5); }
  .hero .v-lead { max-width:52rem; }
  .reading-grid, .design-grid, .limits-grid, .sources-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.9fr) minmax(20rem,1.1fr); gap:clamp(3rem,8vw,8rem); align-items:start; }
  .reading-points p { padding:1.2rem 0; margin:0; border-top:1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .results-head { max-width:52rem; margin-bottom:3rem; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x:auto; outline-offset:.3rem; }
  table { width:100%; min-width:48rem; border-collapse:collapse; background:var(--v-paper); color:var(--v-ink); }
  caption { position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; overflow:hidden; clip:rect(0 0 0 0); }
  th, td { padding:1rem; border:1px solid var(--v-line); text-align:left; }
  thead th { background:var(--v-off); color:var(--v-ink); font:600 .875rem/1.3 var(--vf-body); }
  tbody th { font-size:.9rem; }
  td { font:600 var(--vs-label)/1.3 var(--vf-body); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; white-space:nowrap; }
  /* Derived from Forest, not a new hue. The previous rgba(18,255,117,.13) was a bright
     mint that appears nowhere in the palette. */
  td.loaded { background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--v-green) 9%, var(--v-paper)); }
  tr.group th { background:var(--v-line); font:600 .8125rem/1.3 var(--vf-body); }
  .table-note { max-width:55rem; font-size:.85rem; }
  .composite-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr auto; gap:2rem 5rem; align-items:end; }
  .composite-score { display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:flex-end; }
  .composite-score strong { font:600 clamp(3.2rem,9vw,7rem)/.8 var(--v-font-display); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .composite-score span { margin-top:1rem; font:500 var(--vs-label)/1.3 var(--vf-body); color:var(--v-green); }
  .composite-note { grid-column:1/-1; border-top:1px solid var(--v-line); padding-top:1rem; font-size:.85rem; }
  .design-grid ol { list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; }
  .design-grid li { display:grid; grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr; gap:1rem; padding:1.2rem 0; border-top:1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .design-grid li > span { font:600 var(--vs-label)/1.3 var(--vf-body); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; color:var(--v-green); padding-top:.3rem; }
  .design-grid h3, .design-grid p { margin:0; }
  .design-grid p { margin-top:.4rem; color:var(--v-ink-soft); }
  .historical { grid-column:1/-1; padding:1.25rem; border-left:.4rem solid var(--v-green); background:var(--v-white); font-size:.88rem; }
  .design-grid > .v-link { grid-column:2; }
  .integrity-head { max-width:52rem; margin-bottom:3rem; }
  .integrity-head > p:last-child { color:var(--v-ink-soft); }
  .issues { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr); border-top:1px solid var(--v-line); border-left:1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .issues li { display:grid; grid-template-columns:2.5rem 1fr; gap:1rem; padding:1.25rem; border-right:1px solid var(--v-line); border-bottom:1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .issues li > span { color:var(--v-green); font:600 var(--vs-label)/1.3 var(--vf-body); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; padding-top:.25rem; }
  .issues summary { cursor:pointer; font-weight:700; }
  .issues p { color:var(--v-ink-soft); font-size:.88rem; }
  .limits-grid ol { list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0; }
  .limits-grid li { display:grid; grid-template-columns:2.5rem 1fr; gap:1rem; border-top:1px solid var(--v-line); padding:1rem 0; }
  .limits-grid li span { font:600 var(--vs-label)/1.3 var(--vf-body); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; color:var(--v-green); padding-top:.45rem; }
  .limits-grid li p { margin:0; }
  .sources-grid dl { margin:0; }
  .sources-grid dl div { display:grid; grid-template-columns:10rem 1fr; gap:1rem; padding:1rem 0; border-top:1px solid var(--v-line); }
  .sources-grid dt { font-weight:700; }
  .sources-grid dd { margin:0; overflow-wrap:anywhere; }
  .source-actions { grid-column:2; display:flex; gap:1.5rem; align-items:center; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  @media (max-width:760px) {
    .reading-grid, .design-grid, .limits-grid, .sources-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .design-grid > .v-link, .source-actions { grid-column:1; }
    .composite-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .composite-score { align-items:flex-start; }
    .issues { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .sources-grid dl div { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:.3rem; }
  }
</style>
